```

## Loading

From the directory containing the finalized `KANADE-v1` folder, load the local AudioFolder:

```python
from datasets import load_dataset

local = load_dataset("audiofolder", data_dir="KANADE-v1", split="train")
sample = local[0]
print(sample["audio"], sample["transcription"], sample["speaker"])
```

The Hub repository is private. Authenticate with a token authorized for `ultemica/kanade-voices` before loading:

```python
from datasets import load_dataset

hub = load_dataset("ultemica/kanade-voices", split="train", token=True)
sample = hub[0]
print(sample["audio"], sample["transcription"], sample["speaker"])
```

`metadata.csv` uses AudioFolder's relative `file_name` linking column, plus `transcription`, `speaker`, `speaker_id`, `utterance_id`, `voice_id`, `source_scn`, `scenario_event_index`, `display_text`, and `quality_flags`. AudioFolder exposes the linked WAV as the `audio` feature in loaded rows.

## Schema

| Field | Type | Meaning |
| --- | --- | --- |
| `file_name` in `metadata.csv` | string | Relative link to the verified WAV; AudioFolder loads it as `audio` |
| `audio` in a loaded row | Audio feature | Decoded or decodable verified WAV |
| `transcription` | string | Normalized Japanese spoken text |
| `speaker` / `speaker_id` | string | Source speaker name and canonical ID |
| `utterance_id` / `voice_id` | string | Stable accepted row and source voice IDs |
| `display_text` | string | Japanese display text before spoken-text normalization |
| `quality_flags` | string | Semicolon-separated review cues; empty when none |

The accepted JSONL manifest also preserves raw Japanese text, source observations, audio hashes, and verified duration.

## Intended Use

This private copy is for research and educational, noncommercial work on Japanese ASR, TTS, and speech analysis. It is not a grant of rights to the game audio or text.

## Data Source & Extraction

The source is the KANADE game data. Voice OGGs were matched to Japanese scenario text through exact source IDs and speaker metadata, converted to mono PCM WAV, and independently checked against the source before this Card was rendered. See the [official KANADE site](https://kanade.frontwing.co.jp/) and the [Nintendo Switch listing](https://www.nintendo.com/us/store/products/kanade-switch/).

## Limitations and Quality Policy

This private dataset contains Japanese audio only. Frontwing states that game text supports Japanese, English, Simplified Chinese, and Traditional Chinese; the protagonist is excluded from full voice. The presence of those text languages does not imply translated audio in this dataset. Ambiguous joins, unsupported markup, and invalid audio are rejected and accounted for in reports. Manual sample decisions bind to a digest of the accepted row, including the WAV hash and text, so changed evidence requires a new decision. Accepted audio is not guaranteed free of performance effects, music, or transcription mistakes.

